From: Luma Developers <dev@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] simple: allow AWB to ignore saturated sensor samples

Adapt the saturated-sample exclusion described and implemented by Martin
Neiva de Carvalho in https://patchwork.libcamera.org/patch/28175/ to the
pinned Simple IPA and existing Luma metering statistics.

Keep existing whole-frame colour sums and luminance histograms unchanged.
Sensor tuning opts into unclipped colour sums using Awb.rejectSaturated.
Subtract black level using only the contributing sample count; retain the
previous white balance if every sample is saturated. Existing calibrated
phone profiles keep their current estimator unless explicitly opted in.

